<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ōnin War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1467">1467</a>–<a href="/years/1477">1477</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Onin War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ōnin War was a civil war fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> from 1467 to 1477, mainly in and around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a>, between factions led by Hosokawa Katsumoto and Yamana Sōzen over the shogunal succession and the inheritance of great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> houses. It left the capital in ruins and broke the authority of the Ashikaga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>, opening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a>, in which provincial lords such as the Asakura seized power for themselves.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/onin-war.jpg" alt="Ōnin War" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utagawa Yoshitora · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Onin-War-1467-1477-The-Battle-of-Onin-by-Utagawa-Yoshitora.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
